{"id":"2026-11-22-AMKR","date":"2026-11-22","ticker":"AMKR","name":"Amkor Technology","sector":"Information Technology","industry":"Semiconductor Equipment & Materials","price":30.24,"price_date":"2026-11-20","timeframe_days":182,"headline":"Amkor's sales growth fell from 26% to zero in one quarter, its outlook points to a drop, and it is about to spend heavily on new plants","side":"short","timeframe":"About 6 months, through the next two quarterly reports","thesis":"Amkor's sales growth fell from 26% in the June quarter to 0.2% in September, the sharpest slowdown of any stock on the short list. The outlook is worse: December quarter sales of $1.9B to $2.0B are about 7% to 9% below a year ago, and earnings per share of $0.65 to $0.75 are below September's $0.76. Its phone-chip business, led by Apple, fell 8% from June, and component shortages hit premium phones and wearables. At the same time Amkor is spending $2.5B on equipment and buildings this year, will spend $400M to $450M on Korea alone in 2027, and has a $12B Arizona campus planned, so cash will be tight while sales slip. The tone on the call cooled: net tone fell by 39 points and management dodged two questions after dodging none the quarter before. The stock has already fallen from 86 to 30, but it keeps making lower highs and sits far under both averages.","wrong_if":"A close above 37.50 would retake the November bounce high and mean sellers are done. The idea is also wrong if the December quarter comes in above the $2.0B top of the guide, or if Amkor lands a large new AI packaging customer that lifts 2027 sales growth back into double digits.","business":"Amkor packages and tests computer chips. Chip designers and chip makers send finished silicon wafers to Amkor, which cuts them into chips, wraps them in protective packages with the wiring that connects them to a circuit board, and tests them. Its biggest markets are smartphones (Apple is the largest customer), computing and data centers, cars and industrial gear, and consumer devices. It runs plants in Korea, the Philippines, China, Taiwan, Malaysia, Vietnam, Japan and Portugal, and is building one in Arizona.","segments_note":"The brief has no segment table for Amkor, so this comes from the call. Communications, mostly smartphones, fell 8% from June. Computing rose 25% from June to a record and should grow more than 50% from a year ago in December, and cars and industrial rose 7% to a record. Consumer rose 10%. So the drop is concentrated in phones, which are the largest market, while AI computing is growing fast but is not yet big enough to offset it.","growth_note":"Sales were $1.99B, up 0.2% from a year ago, after 28% in March and 26% in June. The December guide implies a fall of about 7% to 9%. Margins went the other way so far: gross margin rose to 18.3%, up 4 points from a year ago, and operating margin was 11.3%. The guide calls for 18% to 19% gross margin, so margins are expected to stall as sales fall. Missing: 2027 spending guidance, which management said it will give in February.","commentary":[{"point":"December quarter sales are expected at $1.9B to $2.0B, gross margin 18% to 19%, and earnings per share $0.65 to $0.75.","speaker":"Megan Faust, CFO","call":"Q3 2026","kind":"number"},{"point":"Communications sales fell 8% from June, and component shortages for premium phones and wearables were an added drag.","speaker":"Megan Faust, CFO","call":"Q3 2026","kind":"number"},{"point":"Korea construction will cost about $400M to $450M in 2027, the $12B Arizona campus starts its second phase in late 2027, and spending will step up in 2027. Full 2027 spending guidance comes in February.","speaker":"Kevin Engel, CEO","call":"Q3 2026","kind":"number"},{"point":"Computing sales rose 25% from June to a record and should grow more than 50% from a year ago in December. This is the bull case.","speaker":"Megan Faust, CFO","call":"Q3 2026","kind":"number"},{"point":"Admitted there is definite cost pressure and short-term costs from moving production between plants.","speaker":"Kevin Engel, CEO","call":"Q3 2026","kind":"tone"},{"point":"Said it is too early to tell how the new plant will affect margins, and that its costs will not hit the income statement until it is finished.","speaker":"Megan Faust, CFO","call":"Q3 2026","kind":"tone"},{"point":"Still opened upbeat, calling it a strong quarter with record computing and car sales.","speaker":"Kevin Engel, CEO","call":"Q3 2026","kind":"tone"}],"tone_note":"The opening remarks stayed upbeat, but the overall tone fell. Net tone dropped from 125 to 86, the opening remarks fell from 240 to 117, and management dodged two questions after none the call before. The answers to analysts held steady, so the cooling came mostly from what they chose to say up front. Cautious words like shortages, pressure and too early showed up more.","technical_note":"The stock closed at 30.24, far under its 50-day average (43.75) and 200-day average (56.21), and both averages are falling. It peaked at 96.68 earlier in the year and has fallen about 69% from there, including a 25% drop on July 28. A bounce in early November stalled around 36, and the stock made a new low of 29.95 just before the posted close. RSI is 34, low but not at an extreme. It trails the S&P 500 by 30 points over three months.","valuation_note":"At 12.2 times trailing earnings, Amkor is below its median of 14.9, so it is not expensive. Trailing earnings include the strong first half, though, and the December guide points lower. If earnings fall by a quarter and the multiple stays near 12, the price lands near the target.","levels":{"entry_lo":29,"entry_hi":34,"stop":37.5,"target":18,"note":"Sell short between 29 and 34, from the current price up to the area where the November bounce failed. The stop at 37.50 is above the bounce high of about 36 and about 2.5 daily ranges above the posted price. The target of 18 is near the 2025 lows and assumes earnings fall with sales at a multiple near 12. From the posted price that is about $12 of downside for $7 of risk, or 1.7 to 1."},"risks":["Short squeeze risk: the stock is down about 69% from its high, and any good AI news could spark a fast rally.","Computing is growing more than 50% and could outgrow the phone slump sooner than expected.","A new Apple phone cycle or the end of component shortages could bring phone sales back quickly.","US subsidies for the Arizona plant could ease the cash strain.","Not known from the brief: Amkor's short interest, its 2027 spending plan and the date of the next report."],"catalysts":["The December quarter report, likely in early February 2027, with 2027 spending guidance.","Apple's December quarter results and iPhone build reports.","Updates from AI chip makers on packaging capacity, which could help or hurt the bull case."],"facts":{"financials":{"updated":"2026-11-19","adj_eps_name":null,"quarters":[{"q":"Dec '23","id":"FY2023Q4","end":"2023-12-31","rev":1751.811,"gm":15.9,"om":9.1,"nm":6.7,"eps":0.48,"adj_eps":null,"rev_yoy":-8.1,"eps_yoy":-28.4},{"q":"Mar '24","id":"FY2024Q1","end":"2024-03-31","rev":1365.511,"gm":14.8,"om":5.4,"nm":4.3,"eps":0.24,"adj_eps":null,"rev_yoy":-7.2,"eps_yoy":33.3},{"q":"Jun '24","id":"FY2024Q2","end":"2024-06-30","rev":1461.474,"gm":14.5,"om":5.6,"nm":4.6,"eps":0.27,"adj_eps":null,"rev_yoy":0.2,"eps_yoy":3.8},{"q":"Sep '24","id":"FY2024Q3","end":"2024-09-30","rev":1861.589,"gm":14.6,"om":8.0,"nm":6.6,"eps":0.49,"adj_eps":null,"rev_yoy":2.2,"eps_yoy":-9.3},{"q":"Dec '24","id":"FY2024Q4","end":"2024-12-31","rev":1629.118,"gm":15.1,"om":8.3,"nm":6.5,"eps":0.43,"adj_eps":null,"rev_yoy":-7.0,"eps_yoy":-10.4},{"q":"Mar '25","id":"FY2025Q1","end":"2025-03-31","rev":1321.575,"gm":11.9,"om":2.4,"nm":1.6,"eps":0.09,"adj_eps":null,"rev_yoy":-3.2,"eps_yoy":-62.5},{"q":"Jun '25","id":"FY2025Q2","end":"2025-06-30","rev":1511.392,"gm":12.0,"om":6.1,"nm":3.6,"eps":0.22,"adj_eps":null,"rev_yoy":3.4,"eps_yoy":-18.5},{"q":"Sep '25","id":"FY2025Q3","en